 }
```

The fix adds a check for JS_ATOM_NULL before freeing each atom. This prevents attempting to free null atoms which could cause issues in the atom reference counting system.

The condition `tab[i].atom != JS_ATOM_NULL` will evaluate to true only when there's an actual atom to free, which is when the bug would otherwise be triggered (trying to free a null atom). However, since we're preventing the bug rather than detecting it, we don't need to call `funlogline()` in this case.
